QA round (#105, ADR-0013). First load: upstream's chunk groups let Rolldown pull modules every chunk needs (Vite's
preload helper, the Buffer polyfill, DOMPurify, uuid, dayjs, marked, es-toolkit) into the mermaid chunk, so all pages
imported 3 MB of diagram code statically; a higher-priority `shared-libs` group keeps them apart and mermaid loads only
for a diagram. The service worker no longer precaches the large on-demand chunks (mermaid, HEIC, sandpack); they are
cached on first use. A failed navigation shows the EF offline page (assets/ef-offline.html, handler in
assets/ef-offline-sw.js). The manifest gets a description, an id, a 512 px icon and a new-chat shortcut; iOS gets the
app title. The starter cards carry a hook so short phone screens keep the composer in view (brand.css).

